[PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]
## Consolidated Experience from Similar Tasks
The retrieved experiences all point to a common failure mode: manipulation actions were attempted without first satisfying preconditions. Pick-up actions fail when the object is not near or reachable; place actions fail when the robot is not already holding the object; movement actions fail when the path is blocked. Successful manipulation requires confirming proximity and reachability before grasping, confirming grasp before placing, and checking that movement paths are clear. In general: verify the environment and robot state before each skill, follow the correct sequence (locate/navigate -> approach -> grasp -> verify hold -> manipulate/place), and replan if feedback indicates a precondition is unmet.

## Preliminary Thinking
For 'pick up the pencil carefully and hold it securely': 1) Locate the pencil and confirm it is visible and within reach; if not, navigate toward it and adjust the robot's position until it is within interaction distance. 2) Clear or avoid any obstacles around the pencil and ensure the approach path is unobstructed. 3) Approach carefully, align the gripper with the pencil's graspable part, and execute the pick-up skill. 4) After picking, verify that the robot is actually holding the pencil using sensor, gripper, or visual feedback. 5) If the pick fails, check proximity, reachability, and gripper alignment, then replan and retry. 6) Once held, maintain a secure grasp and avoid movements that could knock it loose; if placing later, confirm the grasp before any place action.
[/PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]